## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region data marketplaces under OTCA governance, including residency enforcement, DP budgeting, and auditability.

## Key Concepts

- Data marketplace catalog and policy engine
- Per-tenant residency and epsilon accounting
- Region-scoped streaming and cross-region aggregation
- Immutable audit logs and billing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation
function evaluateAccess(user, dataset) {
  if (!dataset.policies.includes(user.role)) return false;
  if (Date.now() < dataset.validFrom || Date.now() > dataset.validUntil) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you revoke access and re-compute epsilon budgets in real time?
- How to test utility loss under bursts and evolving policies?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes OTCA design at scale with multi-tenant isolation, live schema migrations, and regulatory redaction.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA telemetry path design
- Per-tenant residency
- Schema evolution and canary migrations
- Data redaction and immutable logs
- Testing live migrations, rollbacks

## Code Example

```javascript
function redactPII(record, fields = ['user_id','email']) {
  const copy = {...record};
  for (const f of fields) {
    if (f in copy) copy[f] = 'REDACTED';
  }
  return copy;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test canary migrations under multi-region clock skew?
- How would you enforce regulatory redaction across evolving schemas?
